# ADS Beast workspace: rules for every call

1. Check the connection first. Call `whoami` before any other tool of the
   adsbeast server. If it fails, the key is missing or revoked: say so and
   stop. Never ask for a key to be pasted into the chat.
2. Amounts are in the currency of the ad account they came from. Name the
   currency next to every figure. Never add up figures from accounts in
   different currencies and never assume dollars.
3. Never retry a failed create. If `execute_prepared_change`,
   `create_campaign_draft`, `create_webhook` or a non-dry-run
   `push_lead_outcomes` errors or times out, look first with
   `get_prepared_change`, `list_campaign_drafts`, `list_proposals` or
   `list_webhooks`, then report
   what exists.
4. Confirm before anything that affects spend. A change takes two calls:
   a prepare tool stores a preview and returns a `preview_id` (single use,
   15 minutes). Show the preview with the current value, the new value and
   the currency, wait for a clear yes, then call `execute_prepared_change`.
5. Executing is not applying. The change then waits for a person to
   approve it in ADS Beast unless the client's write policy applies it; the
   server cannot approve, and a new campaign is created paused. Report the
   state from `get_prepared_change`, never "done" on your own word.
6. An empty list is not a clean result. Say nothing was returned and name
   what was not checked.
7. Use the matching skill for multi-step work (account-audit,
   wasted-spend-hunt, search-terms-negatives, campaign-launch,
   budget-pacing-check, weekly-report, conversion-tracking-check,
   lead-pipeline-review) instead of improvising the order of calls.
